  Symbols are authored in a 960x960 box whose origin sits at the baseline, so the
  viewBox is "0 -960 960 960" and every y is negative. Android's viewport has no
  negative origin, hence the translate: it moves the glyph down into 0..960
  rather than the path being rewritten by hand, which would make the next update
  a transcription exercise.

  Deliberately three files rather than material-icons-extended, which would ship
  every unused icon given isMinifyEnabled = false (§6.3) — see Appendix A.11.
-->
